# Jira QA Failure Bug Creation

When creating a Jira Bug after a Zephyr/Playwright test failure (including dummy/workflow-validation Bugs), complete **all** of the following before reporting done. Do not treat a description mention of a screenshot path as an attachment.

## 1. Attach the failure screenshot to the Bug

- Upload the genuine local failure PNG to the Bug **Attachments** section.
- Prefer Atlassian MCP `uploadAttachmentToJiraIssue` via `executeWrite` (two-phase):
  1. Call with `issueIdOrKey` + absolute `filePath` → run returned `uploadCommand` in shell → capture `data.id` as `fileId`.
  2. Call again with `issueIdOrKey` + `fileId` to attach as a standalone file.
- Verify with `getJiraIssue` using `fields: ["attachment"]` that the filename appears (id, filename, size, mimeType).
- Never substitute path-only text in the description for a real attachment.

## 2. Set Parent

- Set **Parent** to the related User Story when Jira hierarchy allows.
- If Jira rejects that Parent (peer issue types), look up the story’s Parent Epic and set that Epic as Parent.
- Always keep a Relates (or equivalent) link to the related story/epic when Parent alone is insufficient or as an additional coverage link.
- In this project, **SCRUM-5 is an Epic**, so Bugs may use Parent `SCRUM-5` directly when that is the related work item.

## 3. Set Start date

- Set **Start date** (`customfield_10015` / field name `Start date`) to the execution date as `YYYY-MM-DD`.
- Use `editJiraIssue` / `createJiraIssue` `additional_fields` or `fields` with that value.

## 4. Set Sprint

- Assign the Bug to the currently **active** Sprint on the SCRUM board.
- Prefer copying the related story/epic’s active Sprint when present.
- On create: `createJiraIssue` with `assignToSprint: "active"` or the numeric sprint id/name.
- On existing issues: `manageJiraSprint` with `action: "addIssues"`, the active `sprintId`, and `issueIdsOrKeys`.
- Do not create, start, or close sprints as part of failure-Bug creation.

## 5. Safety and linking (unchanged)

- Keep Zephyr test-case and execution issue links.
- For intentional dummy/workflow Bugs, use label `qa-automation-dummy` and clear DUMMY labeling in the summary/description.
- Do not modify protected regression cases (e.g. SCRUM-T28–T53) or cycle SCRUM-R1 unless the user explicitly asks.
